{"title":"2026 Bespoked Dresden Picks 02: Avalanche, Black Sheep, Drust, La Fraise, Stolen, Vanwoid – John Watson","link":"https://theradavist.com/2026-bespoked-dresden-02","date":1789452358000,"content":"<p><em>Guten morgen! We’re back in Saxony at the Flughafen Dresden for the <a href=\"https://theradavist.com/tag/2026-bespoked-dresden\" target=\"_blank\">2026 Bespoked Dresden</a> showcase. Paul and John spent the weekend at the world’s largest framebuilder showcase, selecting bikes to document for The Radavist’s coverage of the event. Check out our second batch of picks from Avalanche, Black Sheep, Drust, La Fraise, Stolen, and Vanwoid below!</em><span></span></p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/ebb7c54176cb4aaf0f8f957e5b0a844e595f1b183f6f4b694f075ada2f084d6a.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/ed93b1e8cbe71ec687954cadfea70d321b09ed4e5425a07f9e22d39bf24aebd7.jpg 640w, /media/ebb7c54176cb4aaf0f8f957e5b0a844e595f1b183f6f4b694f075ada2f084d6a.jpg 1800w, /media/eb957b527998abd226cde9cde6842a9532033731b4c2febfe2a5b14e3cfa3fc1.jpg\" /></p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/3277ec33520b3a2b162b7826feb0f7c2f95a7a33e18549f595302ea3f26799b8.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/2867b1cdd288d0c600d47dcc8796db33b39d1a9082ebb760f4609b1e75fd87c5.jpg 640w, /media/3277ec33520b3a2b162b7826feb0f7c2f95a7a33e18549f595302ea3f26799b8.jpg 1800w, /media/e5000cdf6848d19b54ce7579a7a641ac3c1f0c9c52ce1212e6b9fe5e81fc9a36.jpg\" /></p>\n<p><strong>The Radavist thanks <a href=\"https://www.brooksengland.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Brooks England</a> for sponsoring our 2025 Bespoked Dresden coverage and our independent Reportage!</strong></p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/f82df1a897564d191f5f6df2026bfb1f9bc80d310d06b4ed0af47baf1c705d58.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/84da1a82652c0e601a41600f2a2440e90865f8aa710493783c74ffbe710f8a83.jpg 640w, /media/f82df1a897564d191f5f6df2026bfb1f9bc80d310d06b4ed0af47baf1c705d58.jpg 1800w, /media/2b30ef0f418bcd86f51d35ff5271f362a911959506358ae238e14f5363ed968f.jpg\" /></p>\n<h3><a href=\"https://www.avalanche-cycles.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Avalanche Cycles</a> Titanium Gravel Bike – John Watson</h3>\n<p>Paris, France-based Avalanche Cycles is a favorite. Marie Kervella and Laurent Beurriand consistently turn out exceptional bikes packed with beautiful details. This year, their razzle dazzle camouflage-inspired gravel bike stopped me in my tracks. Notice how the disruptive pattern flows seamlessly from frame to bags.</p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/c59254f4d59c5fd2add96b2a6384a397e525310221a15a0df7d12d40375b9fc5.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/3bd2ecb74e7fba7f611a7127e7d55437fcfa966415e8896174f928a8e0f63761.jpg 640w, /media/c59254f4d59c5fd2add96b2a6384a397e525310221a15a0df7d12d40375b9fc5.jpg 1800w, /media/a9e3eb09668d0e49fcb97e0e5373b17da963c5228f5f6a549e3646b8094cebde.jpg\" /></p>\n<p>In order to do so, Laurent and Marie had to envision the geometric overlays in 3D CAD. Then, the maker behind <a href=\"https://coprabikepacking.com/About\" target=\"_blank\">Copra Bags</a> ensured the pattern lines continued onto the surface by overlaying fabric; the design is not printed on the material. This level of detailing is profoundly time-consuming, but the result is nothing short of show-stopping.</p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/174b6012194919980f7722e635aadb09a3a3d44dab654d85f1a97aff079e22b6.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/c7c59a518dbaf684a3873e29b5dcc40255395f76552cf5bdfa6c9d91fb276a9a.jpg 800w, /media/174b6012194919980f7722e635aadb09a3a3d44dab654d85f1a97aff079e22b6.jpg 1600w, /media/c6212f2e07624e6bd0567c8b0bbf755fd9ff36fc672b8bd417355b94dcabdd35.jpg\" /><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/117ca3022daf7a17aeffe25a0714de092096a3f6d7db09e4203c4eea617538b2.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/eb96a5afe8dd2cbd68bc5ee37da8b63bc395f326d19a8aa95b4804cba8a35855.jpg 800w, /media/117ca3022daf7a17aeffe25a0714de092096a3f6d7db09e4203c4eea617538b2.jpg 1600w, /media/a93ddbc24eb73d51a255fa57cb85731e13506c2b43ec82949f551e5caacee41c.jpg\" /><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/7eea57922a9d4ed6b6be2c9af0dae37ad4578376c5dc8d688eca25341b139520.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/2e80e7f8de5e98b1cd96eded6ad7cbbcdf822911cd45ef622d0246054468bf61.jpg 800w, /media/7eea57922a9d4ed6b6be2c9af0dae37ad4578376c5dc8d688eca25341b139520.jpg 1600w, /media/d50510b960e92dbf53b7ea507169e3eee0b31b75a1bc379143e3d5b7a4b9cdad.jpg\" /></p>\n<p>The details don’t stop at the bags, either. Marie’s fabrication skills on are full display here, with a combination of 3D-printed lugs and traditional tubing used to create one sleek silhouette. After welding, Marie finishes the frame to make the 3D-printed parts blend seamlessly into the welded tubes, with the Avalanche logos and fender/rack mounts remaining on the surface.</p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/fe8392bae805ff2fc2a22860df6f13ac435a7fb0b4796ea9bf9e2c6736877089.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/13b42b888555e8bad2376b64122176b50706afbac9f7b681882e4eb5e9d79a13.jpg 800w, /media/fe8392bae805ff2fc2a22860df6f13ac435a7fb0b4796ea9bf9e2c6736877089.jpg 1600w, /media/19fd576941ee6bea12b0643f934e624e53060b4b8c0b50a93afaa67d78f8f766.jpg\" /><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/beb141e8db27131479cefefe157d7184f8eb63dc4d5916dfd4dc9f52db672acb.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/1515f9fb5d2a7c1eb7dcfbb9e665c1e49b3f2f540ae86c422f7bdc5ad77be3e8.jpg 800w, /media/beb141e8db27131479cefefe157d7184f8eb63dc4d5916dfd4dc9f52db672acb.jpg 1600w, /media/65bf828af04ff88fe2937de1197bb2328735e712032d0d8ce0bc522ddc3f40b9.jpg\" /><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/43f3aefff63f3526840c04dc1f8801c700df352c5ac59875d47c91a81b538248.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/ca4ada4186e1f637373ae37d49d9aa0d118f5ff4ac055cb801a3f62bb2f2c59b.jpg 800w, /media/43f3aefff63f3526840c04dc1f8801c700df352c5ac59875d47c91a81b538248.jpg 1600w, /media/15f08dbb0fc15daac3d3bc98a19b8dc811049a4441fe26b7d0e4bae43e98bd2a.jpg\" /></p>\n<p>Throughout the frame, other details show an attentive, considerate approach to 3D modeling and fabrication, fully utilizing modern technologies to make a more functional frame. The notched brake mount, fork crown, and chainstay yoke are all emblematic of Avalanche’s approach to bicycle design.</p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/49e82d85f054166699d96f3e9d91a369378ea3c0e682d77e51205dfa6e86738a.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/a77cc66d0890566cea62f1a7e66df5d5b088013815ab868a168a4d1cd4293c59.jpg 640w, /media/49e82d85f054166699d96f3e9d91a369378ea3c0e682d77e51205dfa6e86738a.jpg 1800w, /media/f077cc48c238cae8bb51d086d1d12f649266cff8011d33f6aa0171a0bc3cf0b0.jpg\" /></p>\n<p>Marie, it was lovely to connect this year. Well done.</p>\n<h3><a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/avalanchecycles/?hl=en\" target=\"_blank\">@AvalancheCycles</a></h3>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/4fb1893a24caf3a4c12e786a850219ae70603b3cab898d56cc1a9228e625c38f.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/b6d0dcd0800502b04b345bdade14c72e8cd357f484040793bc9e66b51eb65c90.jpg 640w, /media/4fb1893a24caf3a4c12e786a850219ae70603b3cab898d56cc1a9228e625c38f.jpg 1800w, /media/5e747275e092fa0a2da75424559278c12dfb064d986128f838dea375b5fc09ff.jpg\" /></p>\n<h3><a href=\"https://www.blacksheepbikes.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Black Sheep Bikes</a> Mixte Commuter – John Watson</h3>\n<p>Hailing from Fort Collins, Colorado, Black Sheep Bicycles is a family operation. James Bleakley’s son Tarryn was in attendance displaying his latest bicycle creation. Last year, I picked the <a href=\"https://theradavist.com/2025-bespoked-dresden-01#:~:text=Black%20Sheep%20Titanium%20Soft%20Tail%20Coaster%20Cruiser\" target=\"_blank\">flex pivot coaster brake mountain bike</a> for “Best Off-Road”; this year, Tarryn brought his new commuter mixte.</p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/e7abd2e5ce63925517af5cec1f4f0c8447f42934df90e3b9bd78e6dbcb7ee9d8.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/08bc1c08e4d15d3e4cd995662cf40957393ed55bc402c5fd562a2ceeaf811b35.jpg 800w, /media/e7abd2e5ce63925517af5cec1f4f0c8447f42934df90e3b9bd78e6dbcb7ee9d8.jpg 1600w, /media/081b5a4ecc0b34e1ca5f0785bb66e1aa1a277acdfdd3a9eacd8d3f6139a361e7.jpg\" /><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/ca9c3122fa03dc2c70c6d75243ad37ecf094125ff632c764afd1d33561d85aba.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/0dd214bb64f41251aa64167d68d7ac740c61b6b54a0cf24588c6a198d5803db9.jpg 800w, /media/ca9c3122fa03dc2c70c6d75243ad37ecf094125ff632c764afd1d33561d85aba.jpg 1600w, /media/1843fc1632db1d0da22b6bc387129e7dfe546034d6d227deed486e3926573fe9.jpg\" /><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/cff6bdca0d3a4f8516c133f063cd34503c119256dd46cf873365fab46e039921.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/39cc5b8bae41afb8b149f24bc982891a867129d4f2a5a419c207b523a2c66d99.jpg 800w, /media/cff6bdca0d3a4f8516c133f063cd34503c119256dd46cf873365fab46e039921.jpg 1600w, /media/2bd7f769400dba494d5da80671d81707ec9d91a44e1ff0ff33f8b5ff3d14d9d1.jpg\" /></p>\n<p>Because it’s a commuter bike, Tarryn wanted front and rear racks, so we’ll start at the front. This demi porteur rack features a grid made of titanium rods that pass through the rack’s structure, with each rod woven in an under/over pattern. Long struts mount just above the dropout on the fork and on top of the segmented shoulders of the fork.</p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/cd0995deeea51b012384f53efd52616459fa7c02ffd385679e37ee88346cc2ca.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/ad4a39fed24bd045d9cb9f4d2bcf50d080f2520d9d7e635225d154048b2c3b07.jpg 800w, /media/cd0995deeea51b012384f53efd52616459fa7c02ffd385679e37ee88346cc2ca.jpg 1600w, /media/1e6c6cfb74833aaac2902be11c2b50116b5532fd5abde562f755d76c71c48222.jpg\" /><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/b97673eb433ba0d30e3d9c6f55373f76762e9f6579dcab1de7b05a29b11eb26e.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/62e8613957bc8e9605ce8ada4b8ddbcc6be2cf93d26e3a7e5e3db1befd6a5c4a.jpg 800w, /media/b97673eb433ba0d30e3d9c6f55373f76762e9f6579dcab1de7b05a29b11eb26e.jpg 1600w, /media/eba75a1e36f95cad8a85997a54aee1bf02b907ba24bfc9bbcdaa0a5b5971c864.jpg\" /><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/ce0a80fddb0f77e1959fce0cd6f73b33393ed2c4843f2ebe3dc75fcdc16d9113.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/bf73d562023ee28987d90245b0300a2e1b51663726a2d5913cf5cf8b794753bc.jpg 800w, /media/ce0a80fddb0f77e1959fce0cd6f73b33393ed2c4843f2ebe3dc75fcdc16d9113.jpg 1600w, /media/8ec4c8affac29549d79e6ad5f7308b8f05b10ddc2485545f5a6132d28e1166f3.jpg\" /></p>\n<p>Once Tarryn completed the double top tube mixte bar’s attachment at the rear dropout, he added spider web details for stiffeners. Liking the design, he included them in the rear rack. This rack also features a cupped platform to hold his yoga mat more easily.</p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/55bf725a36963eab1f77b6fbac8c29237af23174614b4693ee381e7313ed7b46.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/7c3b363c8745c4b355e935fa7f391b54ef6c97071983bd3329e8c8a88f433da3.jpg 640w, /media/55bf725a36963eab1f77b6fbac8c29237af23174614b4693ee381e7313ed7b46.jpg 1800w, /media/1281d8042b232471daf1acb67cf77a3b81106143c05f5dd89e7aba6edd72cd6a.jpg\" /></p>\n<p>I love seeing what creation Tarryn concocts each year at Bespoked! Well done!</p>\n<h3><a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/blacksheepbikes/?hl=en\" target=\"_blank\">@BlackSheepBikes</a></h3>\n<p> </p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/8af2914641697a3515e6a8cbd50cddcfe051e7f468958c601bcf2036332891bf.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/972feafb0405b8670b6dc6ae7a08fc88b8906f58dbc86b5dba2a7db83e7eb93c.jpg 640w, /media/8af2914641697a3515e6a8cbd50cddcfe051e7f468958c601bcf2036332891bf.jpg 1800w, /media/cc172bd838f01897ba84e6bd180c51d28fc73db24d5dd02cea76b57460bcb0fc.jpg\" /></p>\n<h3><a href=\"https://drustcycles.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Drust Cycles</a> Wheelbarrow – John Watson</h3>\n<p>“Did I tell you about the dude ordering a custom wheelbarrow?” was how Konstantin Drust began our daily text thread one afternoon. And no lie, a few months later, this thing shows up. Berlin-based Drust Cycles is all about pushing the boundaries at a bike show, but this takes the definition of “bicycle” and blurs the lines. Using his signature thick fillet fabrication style, the builder began constructing the bike with a series of large bends and stiffened up the design as needed with bracing.</p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/b950f23a0088676829f983844acaf63e8003ba135d8a294e8a06b83fb19a09e6.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/62161a60b3ca963787af112e6fe71823c758524cf33166c0e828b9c3f9e33b5a.jpg 800w, /media/b950f23a0088676829f983844acaf63e8003ba135d8a294e8a06b83fb19a09e6.jpg 1600w, /media/0fb38f761960cbf98b96e488e71d1177bfbe66c8a18305a5c8e3d53f48952745.jpg\" /><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/f4e3ff06b006b6e48811b3beb0fae1f1d9e1fd6814076d9cdc03bea34222ff9a.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/5d73cb4ec81e45c0ab4c51a1b4742f03209b0567426a5a711822388337ab6d7b.jpg 800w, /media/f4e3ff06b006b6e48811b3beb0fae1f1d9e1fd6814076d9cdc03bea34222ff9a.jpg 1600w, /media/986a8a29e8abbf7076e12585d0812f1658114a5cc90743575b57e32f492799ef.jpg\" /><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/dff14f42078572783c72bc86ca29cc1ef439d1c10dcd022727c5deaa3638a814.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/787ec978f7a88a8552f43eee8974385342f5f940ea0c8d7fc134ea3b7a9c053c.jpg 800w, /media/dff14f42078572783c72bc86ca29cc1ef439d1c10dcd022727c5deaa3638a814.jpg 1600w, /media/759cddbd7bdf103cfd11da18628b11c2bc867b698af0b330221fed30d38af83a.jpg\" /></p>\n<p>Where it gets ridiculous is the front wheel, which was supplied by Velocity’s German distributor, <a href=\"https://munrowheels.de/\" target=\"_blank\">Munro Wheels</a>, who laced the splatter-anodized 20″ rim to a bright orange Erase hub. Then, for a brake – because every wheelbarrow needs a brake, right? Hayes Dominion A4s in the limited brown finish offer wheel-skidding power for heavy loads.</p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/91b2d772060e6d9fa5b3c7136db93c585875aff41cf3e5934af9a24abf642182.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/f7897c47bc3dff9c0ce728c2461d3b91efda9851e58c4b61ede9c4fdc83a45ec.jpg 800w, /media/88cc05107b02817584f955a813e976ca2b2b7a502bfcdf65c001c76d6f1b2954.jpg 1600w, /media/91b2d772060e6d9fa5b3c7136db93c585875aff41cf3e5934af9a24abf642182.jpg\" /><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/87754e748861a0621b16af4040307a5c2971d76aae04008f75b1dcd6d2fa5bf1.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/b3b738aae0b825da3fe016556801c46027fc1732132460c4045134d3978223ce.jpg 800w, /media/4c6eb870715fb8a86c02beb96be3f18f4ee298defee881b05df5bee6955fc29c.jpg 1600w, /media/87754e748861a0621b16af4040307a5c2971d76aae04008f75b1dcd6d2fa5bf1.jpg\" /></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.sq-lab.com/en/product-category/bike-grips-and-handlebar-tapes\" target=\"_blank\">SQ Lab ergonomic grips</a> and a <a href=\"https://silca.cc/en-eu/products/impero-ultimate-frame-pump\" target=\"_blank\">Silca Impero Ultimate II frame pump</a> are two more over-the-top details on this extravagant garden tool. Oh yeah, and two bottle cages – because why not?</p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/bfec3ee4ae0663ec414b8eba9c1b35d6c7bcddc4b0228b4b4bdbe1ce3adee1a8.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/211a4bc205dfac0df86816564e931c96812ace0ff6a721cb262931620aa85aed.jpg 640w, /media/bfec3ee4ae0663ec414b8eba9c1b35d6c7bcddc4b0228b4b4bdbe1ce3adee1a8.jpg 1800w, /media/00daaf5f0ac5d82f91f243d9f15dcfaea572bc47e38bd4a1a6036c78f8f50f9c.jpg\" /></p>\n<p>This is the sort of ridiculousness that is always a welcome distraction. Thanks to Kata from Rasch Cycles for modeling the barrow’s use!</p>\n<h3><a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/drustcycles/?hl=en\" target=\"_blank\">@DrustCycles</a></h3>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/432054064acf8ae4f8bfbd4581c3b0607bb63e8e5148326d839ef3c497b47f02.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/217a6f5440caa6933041c703631d7796a2ddc2e54ee84bc4feda5e981ad309f9.jpg 640w, /media/432054064acf8ae4f8bfbd4581c3b0607bb63e8e5148326d839ef3c497b47f02.jpg 1800w, /media/38ebb71955e9ed9e0fb3aa7ae5fb3b110f8d9503790664f89ec37bc3c3c1946a.jpg\" /></p>\n<h3><a href=\"https://www.lafraisecycles.com/\" target=\"_blank\">LaFraise Cycles</a> Randonneur – John Watson</h3>\n<p>Roubaix-based LaFraise Cycles owner Andreas Behrens commented, “This is the lugged version of <a href=\"https://theradavist.com/2025-bespoked-dresden-picks-05#:~:text=LaFraise%20Cycles%20Tourer\" target=\"_blank\">the bike you shot last year</a>,” as we wheeled this cotton candy ombré-faded beaut of a bicycle through the crowded 2026 Bespoked Dresden showcase.</p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/ace644b3ab86ae1f35f6088a13846e1ad76b676ecbe1425c79026bedf0c45614.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/e9797814fe429d6617329c3d686d1c1f844c28af18e35810830c90dc1b9fc337.jpg 800w, /media/4148c4c2ef8bf8dbc59bd64dd9bfdcc076be8e3b2438c69403cda62a760581d6.jpg 1600w, /media/ace644b3ab86ae1f35f6088a13846e1ad76b676ecbe1425c79026bedf0c45614.jpg\" /><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/a775525f8b596bddf240dbad954266a8656c33f342c12b26fd41bd039ae6bfa9.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/be0a3a4f4c094532d7aa180a8c48e605423d0258799f6178a72c2aa1487cadec.jpg 800w, /media/fb8d988c2363c1defc4b745bacd49f29df6704e822c837341fe873574f2a0484.jpg 1600w, /media/a775525f8b596bddf240dbad954266a8656c33f342c12b26fd41bd039ae6bfa9.jpg\" /></p>\n<p>Andres continued, “I wanted to build a new, lugged frame for this year’s show to experiment with my powdercoater, as well as the new Tim Tas Rek bags and the Cycles Manivelle bikepacking basket.” The powdercoat finish is laid down across the whole frame, and then the headtube is vacuumed clean before being filled with another color. It’s all then clear-coated, giving it a candy finish.</p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/15cf320cdba5b8a66b5880b9b7480bb01f90f07489005b584467a1ee6c3cbf73.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/7771fe374fb0a4485cc994622f073d505fb0125a739c2cee45d9c9d9b405bfd3.jpg 800w, /media/15cf320cdba5b8a66b5880b9b7480bb01f90f07489005b584467a1ee6c3cbf73.jpg 1600w, /media/7b9a6bd67c1cc0a7462ad584fd7dc4c6bf19d6f57dec31fd0249818c56da7a64.jpg\" /><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/8ec7a9fd0c72d45ab98a276f7928c4b0333b436de580ab85dfb1f388c138b234.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/8f7f1ef6f49c42096c3d0d0972f2bbd48b660d0db647797a63efab63ec80317f.jpg 800w, /media/8ec7a9fd0c72d45ab98a276f7928c4b0333b436de580ab85dfb1f388c138b234.jpg 1600w, /media/6c482f49ac3ffb85cab337dbb9c906d3dacf621c252f964236edf3d000aaad6b.jpg\" /><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/ed81a54da2ce1799898f45444e1db5742c8eb01be1c05ce32c11ae606253d3b2.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/a73149bb8e23176f094bd1b0d950f27285aba818a805259c007e21b1fd843fd0.jpg 800w, /media/ed81a54da2ce1799898f45444e1db5742c8eb01be1c05ce32c11ae606253d3b2.jpg 1600w, /media/38e71732c57096d2a4a0c85eadb38a79a7471937018c0d213c3d09e30ffd3208.jpg\" /></p>\n<p>Careful considerations show throughout the bike, with the elegant seat stay bridge diameter closely matching the bag support and direct mounts for the Manivelle basket, ensuring a stable, solid fit.</p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/4442b39dfb0fcf5de214a9711ca953df8c546ca77090944a4f204d35ae9e1add.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/c7b09e12e2911d53f7b9601c4ff789a95b41af91b0bf7762e16add8b3fa907fa.jpg 800w, /media/07ca249fb1e8368dbd18bb658a39a94ab0839db6eb1fb9fc91e4aa35ca4948bf.jpg 1600w, /media/4442b39dfb0fcf5de214a9711ca953df8c546ca77090944a4f204d35ae9e1add.jpg\" /><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/809ab052a6d759ba15a15179d4bf485281b5f7be2e3ea5210c161f05ac003a0b.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/a0f9140236f85cadbf5ca9885a477a6a2a9f9811e56c94c8e3c602da4c66c9af.jpg 800w, /media/3d75a521079a63a994bad059adced9c4601e085d1ce72951ef969f406442310a.jpg 1600w, /media/809ab052a6d759ba15a15179d4bf485281b5f7be2e3ea5210c161f05ac003a0b.jpg\" /></p>\n<p>The <a href=\"https://www.etsy.com/nl/shop/TIMTAS\" target=\"_blank\">Tim Tas Rek</a> bags connect securely and detach quickly from the bike, designed for long-distance, mixed-terrain riding.</p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/5bbbea7831d5d942b885d461d63b445b6a0a39e658e3abfb3f9bf3c4d6fc8b4d.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/1f1c5b0e2f51c230d67e1137dd2af0385d71084edcf9d60175b31ddd71ff7b44.jpg 640w, /media/5bbbea7831d5d942b885d461d63b445b6a0a39e658e3abfb3f9bf3c4d6fc8b4d.jpg 1800w, /media/211d61eb522c8c15c61736fb2e99b76bf8c57a17e4cc4505095aa66dd757504e.jpg\" /></p>\n<p>I love the stark difference between the earth tone, drab-colored bike from last year’s Bespoked Dresden and this year’s brightly-colored offering. Well done!</p>\n<h3><a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/lafraisecycles/\" target=\"_blank\">@LaFraiseCycles</a> <a href=\"https://www.etsy.com/nl/shop/TIMTAS\" target=\"_blank\">@TimTasRek</a></h3>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/0567d3f722b89c8956aa4b3c520e650707a24213ce25f5c36ba927ccbb8612f6.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/85190634dd646448af01dd5a6a0590ac59c32440864215f242eeef91a1671658.jpg 640w, /media/0567d3f722b89c8956aa4b3c520e650707a24213ce25f5c36ba927ccbb8612f6.jpg 1800w, /media/b9de5daa4f31b9acad091b468a9183b7aa5f9d54f2dab77d52db95ef5f9038e0.jpg\" /></p>\n<h3><a href=\"https://www.stolengarage.cc/\" target=\"_blank\">Stolen Garage</a> Two Face Adventure Gravel – John Watson</h3>\n<p>In the 19th arrondissement of Paris, France, lies a cafe, bike shop, and framebuilding operation called <a href=\"https://theradavist.com/stolen-garage-paris-shop-visit\">Stolen Garage</a>. For the 2026 Bespoked Dresden show, Fin and Romain displayed this split-tone adventure gravel bike. The drive side was clear-coated with a splatter design, and the other side was painted black.</p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/1a7c1d9411d01069bbb04bc45ec93062dee81a483590e63cbef84aa850759046.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/d7e20b71d6afa80f0590ebc7208105ce9466e69b494bb06284e03386eb6b22e8.jpg 800w, /media/285f1e3bfd120c1b648403ff0b3d30103cb4ae6f960b52eeb82afc0b890d8884.jpg 1600w, /media/1a7c1d9411d01069bbb04bc45ec93062dee81a483590e63cbef84aa850759046.jpg\" /><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/f916c4e3b32dd133a0bc88e2995ecf59790c85906d68bb9eb156c59e078acbf1.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/9d9d331203e7879d72636746d7ca892bf718a1e9b2abf718df82824ef6700f5e.jpg 800w, /media/3652dd5975410844a0070df6082c07035e6a5324b3b11b21c776d87227624f02.jpg 1600w, /media/f916c4e3b32dd133a0bc88e2995ecf59790c85906d68bb9eb156c59e078acbf1.jpg\" /></p>\n<p>Stolen’s approach to the “two face” finish embodies a duality of serious playfulness, with the drive side being random, fun, and erratic, while the non-drive side is more serious and subdued.</p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/889187b982c02dbd59c31f041ee983895063ecc3887c96225b23b9f852ce08ab.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/f583235a469be217af96b99ed8175d8a283355743d39cd30093b5b53c0330472.jpg 800w, /media/889187b982c02dbd59c31f041ee983895063ecc3887c96225b23b9f852ce08ab.jpg 1600w, /media/3b4a39f5007d4f085ecdb3d0f7dedfef50080c55cc08024d558d6a98f6ef5e13.jpg\" /><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/0fd459039ef002cf3cf6bf129cfccc5c71099c337a5a4ce508c32a08d3aa08ec.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/2a71338afddabbea4b963b530c8e6bc977be8221c03d9384e587a757d85bcbbc.jpg 800w, /media/0fd459039ef002cf3cf6bf129cfccc5c71099c337a5a4ce508c32a08d3aa08ec.jpg 1600w, /media/8f787408a62e04419e6cb45c40b4e01e5b471432f96d523036bca42409740420.jpg\" /><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/5abbc4bb176c8e47354528f538d8ebf22b222a9f47bd1129ab241ddac278cdbd.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/9464b188edfa60ba23d38a0ac3d09e3ebb5ab99636edd5340b98a95174fa60de.jpg 800w, /media/5abbc4bb176c8e47354528f538d8ebf22b222a9f47bd1129ab241ddac278cdbd.jpg 1600w, /media/410f9b0cb455d4a6ff9f5d1090ed6ade48f9ba0072c27fd2063f76268730b5fc.jpg\" /></p>\n<p>Yet the framebuilders didn’t stop there with the creativity. A beautiful segmented fork, with internal cable routing, Konga chainstay yoke, and an asymmetric seat stay bridge perches above a perfectly aligned rear end. This non-boost frame maintains a road drivetrain but floats atop Ultradynamico Mars 29er tires for extra cushioning.</p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/91422d2ce531702bd9f591fe571ca38c7500c1d37acbe093f1d9462719197379.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/18ece4ca7e7777f269e2865a6633750be3f2366366d7c5d330c2de670d7dcb12.jpg 640w, /media/91422d2ce531702bd9f591fe571ca38c7500c1d37acbe093f1d9462719197379.jpg 1800w, /media/d924f36aa23fffe8630f64ba1994362c789bebe5d52bbf9db5db91c6c1fb0f8e.jpg\" /></p>\n<p>Well done, you two. This is a stunning bike!</p>\n<h3><a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/stolengarage/?hl=en\" target=\"_blank\">@StolenGarage</a></h3>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/9f8cc82fb7177d320e00b0b623a3b36d91b2759d82cbd1250b01acfe054953b0.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/adb7805ef8334991aceb307c5874b60796fc48fc65604f40e7c268cdd07b69e4.jpg 640w, /media/9f8cc82fb7177d320e00b0b623a3b36d91b2759d82cbd1250b01acfe054953b0.jpg 1800w, /media/ad1bffaf8acf816d0dc3c48372c2a0baed34f5984650a6a5f92eb8724fc582f8.jpg\" /></p>\n<h3><a href=\"https://www.vanwoid.com/bikes/canapee\" target=\"_blank\">Vanwoid Cycles Canapee</a> Titanium Gravel – John Watson</h3>\n<p>Ollie from Vanwoid, a small builder out of Bayerisch Eisenstein in Germany’s Bavarian Forest, displayed this stunning Canapee adventure gravel bike, named after the mountain range in his village. The Canapee frame clears a 29 x 2.3″ tire while maintaining a non-boost drivetrain thanks to the dropped chainstay design.  As Ollie put it, “We put a drop bar front end on a mountain bike rear end.”</p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/e6829d551fd3dbb2172aa890fda37a35307454c63f4f13196c2538e4a746c921.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/a52310b305546a817ddeb495de576004dc707cfc21ee563c8af48d08eb654c9d.jpg 800w, /media/e6829d551fd3dbb2172aa890fda37a35307454c63f4f13196c2538e4a746c921.jpg 1600w, /media/02b141b90f913d0e42f2465929e7c4905c90a87f776cc6256b4871822b789ece.jpg\" /><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/6130b7ab5ea7e659ad8958e1f634c41005fe2a79727b5ce8efbc636b4c848c44.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/c6c72dbcb111161ffc4b76b32667eddd62c57bc3a59c135d3959fe435eedc65a.jpg 800w, /media/6130b7ab5ea7e659ad8958e1f634c41005fe2a79727b5ce8efbc636b4c848c44.jpg 1600w, /media/872a23de6a19f6587497ae103320936ef69f15658bf1c87d5a3c6ebeaf281f1a.jpg\" /><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/f9ff385038d4eaa32b6418abe066e861142443662e9425369199c131d216bdb0.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/18069bc5dedf8afba37c66c451d092328aa6c7cf406c6d8daaa0a3f36a43e49b.jpg 800w, /media/f9ff385038d4eaa32b6418abe066e861142443662e9425369199c131d216bdb0.jpg 1600w, /media/6607a3bc4171ac893f5a5beca2b271315075114ac03f25122977c80bca428286.jpg\" /></p>\n<p>The Canapee features a titanium gravel fork with 2.4″ clearance. The aesthetic details on this subdued frame are executed in an effortless way. Rolling on Schwalbe G-One RS/RX Pro tires should keep the rubber side down while descending mountain passes on rough alpine roads.</p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/08eccc11fc20104597339d91ca6db04fdc78e26ee37003c3b8568628f082e1a0.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/8279ac3bb7411c90f83dc669710ce06479e2de11762fe255e06d2abb97dfcaeb.jpg 800w, /media/f2e84c23eefde0a23eb91a66795db1c2ddc2efc268fde144b6203b75498fe02c.jpg 1600w, /media/08eccc11fc20104597339d91ca6db04fdc78e26ee37003c3b8568628f082e1a0.jpg\" /><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/d8c16b8b70713398c7d7c25e6ecb1cb9380c4575ed023e2934083dcf1078a9d4.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/c6ee38a0e1b2c684f3914160dbe78d8b9c33c676236467d89c8cd1f443138c6f.jpg 800w, /media/93b81cc633d586bb3830aa62fd2a3b537f90e3c56263a862f4cf1540e9ca4faa.jpg 1600w, /media/d8c16b8b70713398c7d7c25e6ecb1cb9380c4575ed023e2934083dcf1078a9d4.jpg\" /></p>\n<p>For a bike so subdued, the cerakoted bottle bosses match the neon lining of the frame bag. Ollie was proud of this bike but was REALLY proud of the neon details.</p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/46285da6a181a343d386c82acce708a68e5daf9e90cf70122cf480c92f3495e7.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/f68e29c945b8a76fb39d11bb07495ad1e22829c98e5df295f85b1c2a0a713e91.jpg 640w, /media/46285da6a181a343d386c82acce708a68e5daf9e90cf70122cf480c92f3495e7.jpg 1800w, /media/752f5bc3bb145ff8036490713f299ae15da651a9248daa7560d044d486166cca.jpg\" /></p>\n<p>Looks great, Ollie. Well done, mate!</p>\n<h3><a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/vanwoid_cycles/\" target=\"_blank\">@VanwoidCycles</a></h3>\n<p><strong>The Radavist thanks <a href=\"https://www.brooksengland.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Brooks England</a> for sponsoring our 2025 Bespoked Dresden coverage and our independent Reportage!</strong></p>\n<p><strong>We’ve got a lot more on the way, so stay tuned. Which bike could you see yourself riding? Let us know in the comments!</strong></p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://theradavist.com/2026-bespoked-dresden-02\">2026 Bespoked Dresden Picks 02: Avalanche, Black Sheep, Drust, La Fraise, Stolen, Vanwoid</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://cms.theradavist.com/\">The Radavist</a>.</p>","author":"John Watson","comments":"https://theradavist.com/2026-bespoked-dresden-02#comments","siteTitle":"The Radavist","siteHash":"96eb481d8084f04a4602bac57874ba717baf56b758f45547b5caf2312da766ef","entryHash":"ae9db064945c8c1ea8d47d6e6466b09b3b6851ba1b6820b4d4a1f934b9a3032a","category":"Cycling"}